A library (`.doo`) no longer leaves out members on which the user wrote `{:auto_generated}`. Only the members that Dafny itself generates, such as the reveal lemmas of opaque functions, are left out, recognised by their origin rather than by the attribute. Before, a user-written `{:auto_generated}` member that shadowed an imported name disappeared from the stored program, its uses resolved to the imported declaration, and a client could prove false from the library's contracts. The same origin test now decides two other questions the attribute decided: a trait lemma on which the user wrote `{:opaque_reveal}` must be implemented by the classes that extend the trait (before, it need not be, and a call to it assumed its postcondition), and `dafny audit` reports `{:axiom}` and `{:verify false}` on a member on which the user wrote `{:auto_generated}`.
